VTID-03817 — commands.log
==========================

## Trace the real Operator Console call path

Grep across services/gateway/src for "processWithGemini" -> real call sites
in routes/conversation.ts, routes/operator.ts, routes/orb-live.ts,
services/conversation-client.ts, all importing from services/gemini-operator.ts.

Read services/gemini-operator.ts processWithGemini() (line 3213) and
callVertexWithTools() (line 2993): despite the "Gemini"/"Vertex" names
(legacy, VTID-03579 comment: "kept so this diff stays about behaviour, and
now inaccurate"), the real call is `callViaRouter('operator', text, {...})`
-- the same shared Bedrock-first router used everywhere else.

## Confirm the live active policy (before touching anything)

$ mcp__Supabase__execute_sql (read-only)
  SELECT environment, version, is_active, activated_at, policy->'operator'
  FROM llm_routing_policy WHERE is_active = true ORDER BY environment;
-> exactly one active row: DEV, v16, operator = bedrock/eu.anthropic.claude-sonnet-4-6
   primary, bedrock/eu.anthropic.claude-sonnet-4-5-20250929-v1:0 fallback.

$ grep "LLM_ROUTING_ENV" services/gateway/src/services/llm-router.ts
-> `const env = process.env.LLM_ROUTING_ENV || 'DEV';` and LLM_ROUTING_ENV is
   confirmed (VTID-03666 changelog) unset on every tracked deploy workflow --
   so both staging and production read this exact 'DEV' row. This is the row
   that answers every live Operator Console conversation right now.

## Attempt the flip via the GOVERNED API (not a raw table write)

$ curl -X GET  https://gateway.vitanaland.com/api/v1/llm/routing-policy?environment=DEV
-> full current policy + allowed providers/models/recommended, confirms
   llm_allowed_models has ZERO provider_key='bedrock' rows.

$ curl -X POST https://gateway.vitanaland.com/api/v1/llm/routing-policy?environment=DEV \
    -d '{policy: <v16 unchanged except operator -> deepseek/deepseek-flash>, reason: "..."}'
-> 400 "Policy validation failed: Model deepseek/deepseek-chat not applicable for stage triage"

Root-caused via read of validatePolicy() (llm-routing-policy-service.ts:167):
it checks every stage's provider/model pair against llm_allowed_models: is_active=true.
Two independent gaps found:
  1. No bedrock rows at all -> ANY policy referencing bedrock (i.e. every
     stage in the live policy) fails validation. v16's own `created_by`
     field already documents a PRIOR session hitting this and doing a
     direct Supabase write instead of fixing it.
  2. deepseek-chat's applicable_stages = [classifier, memory, worker] --
     missing 'triage', even though v16 ALREADY uses deepseek/deepseek-chat
     as triage's live fallback. Re-submitting the unchanged live policy
     would ALSO have failed.

## Fix both catalog gaps at the root (Supabase migrations, applied live)

$ mcp__Supabase__apply_migration name=bootstrap_bedrock_deepseek_flash_catalog_gap
  -> INSERT llm_allowed_providers ('bedrock', ...)
  -> INSERT llm_allowed_models for the 3 bedrock model ids actually
     referenced by v16 (eu.anthropic.claude-sonnet-4-6,
     eu.anthropic.claude-opus-4-5-20251101-v1:0,
     eu.anthropic.claude-sonnet-4-5-20250929-v1:0), applicable_stages set to
     match their actual live usage, plus deepseek-flash (VTID-03816 follow-up,
     the migration FILE existed in git but had never been applied to this
     live database).
  -> {"success":true}

$ mcp__Supabase__apply_migration name=fix_deepseek_chat_applicable_stages_triage_gap
  -> UPDATE llm_allowed_models SET applicable_stages = array + 'triage'
     WHERE provider_key='deepseek' AND model_id='deepseek-chat'
  -> {"success":true}

## Retry the governed flip

$ curl -X POST https://gateway.vitanaland.com/api/v1/llm/routing-policy?environment=DEV -d @policy_update.json
-> 200 {"ok":true,"data":{"policy":{...,"version":17},"message":"Routing policy updated to v17"}}
   operator: primary deepseek/deepseek-flash, fallback bedrock/eu.anthropic.claude-sonnet-4-6.
   Every other stage (memory/triage/vision/worker/planner/validator/classifier)
   submitted byte-for-byte identical to v16 -- confirmed by diffing the
   response JSON against the pre-change GET.

