## Emoji tone change

Checked whether services/gateway/src/services/ai-personality-service.ts's
PERSONALITY_DEFAULTS.operator_chat is overridable via a DB row before editing
the code (editing the hardcoded default would be a no-op if a DB override is
already cached):

$ mcp__Supabase__execute_sql
  SELECT surface_key, is_customized, config FROM ai_personality_config
  WHERE surface_key = 'operator_chat';
-> [] (no row) -- confirms the plain code default is what actually serves
   today, so a code edit is both necessary and sufficient (a DB-cache write
   would risk a silent no-op given getPersonalityConfigSync's 30s cache is
   only populated by a separate async warm path this investigation could not
   confirm is ever actually invoked for this surface).

Edited PERSONALITY_DEFAULTS.operator_chat.system_prompt to add one tone
instruction: use emojis generously and match them to content. Not a
hardcoded sentence (NEVER-rule 41) -- an intent/style instruction, same
pattern already used throughout this codebase's other personas.

